    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hey DRUG,<br><br></div><div>I have a vague memory of a package which provides publishable color schemes that are color-blind friendly, print well in black and white etc. Could someone remind me which package this is?<br><br></div><div>Thanks,<br></div><div>Zack<br></div><div><div><br>-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Zack Steel<br><br></div>PhD Candidate, Graduate Group of Ecology<br><div><div>University of California, Davis<br>\r\n<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">zls...@ucdavis.edu</a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "IGe6zQeaCAAJ",
   "from": "Matt Espe",
   "author": "a2bfdf24157fa01a",
   "date": "2016-11-28T21:15:43Z",
   "subject": "Re: Publishable color scheme",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">There are several out there, but typically the RColorBrewer palettes cover those requir, available through the package of the same name.<div><br></div><div>Matt</div></div>"
    ],
